  "text": "The Oncology Service - Leesburg | The Oncology Service\nHours & Contact\nTOS - Leesburg\n(571) 209-1176\nleesburg@tosvets.com\nTOS - Richmond\n(804) 999-0001\nrichmond@tosvets.com\nTOS - Springfield\n(703) 451-8900, option 2\nspringfield@tosvets.com\nfacebook\ninstagram\nMenu\nServices\nMedical Oncology\nRadiation Oncology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nStereotactic Radiation Therapy\nOutpatient Imaging\nElectrochemotherapy\nAbout Us\nMeet the Team\nVeterinarians\nTOS Leesburg - Veterinarians\nTOS Richmond - Veterinarians\nTOS Springfield - Veterinarians\nSupport Staff\nTOS Leesburg - Support Staff\nTOS Richmond - Support Staff\nTOS Springfield - Support Staff\nYour First Visit\nWhen Your Pet is a Patient\nPayment Options\nClinical Studies\nCareers\nLeesburg\nRichmond\nSpringfield\nTestimonials\nResources\nForms\nLeesburg Forms\nRichmond Forms\nSpringfield Forms\nFAQs\nPet Chemotherapy Guide\nDiscounts\nGrief Resources\nNutrition For The Canine Oncology Patient\nNutrition For The Feline Oncology Patient\nPet Emergency & Urgent Care Resources\nEvents\nPet Loss Support Group\nPet Cancer Support Group\nBlog\nCats\nDogs\nOther\nLocations\nLeesburg\nLeesburg Referral Form\nLeesburg DVM Referring Form\nRichmond\nSpringfield\nRequest an Appointment\nSearch\nButton Bar\nClient Portal\nrVetLink Portal\nReferral Forms\nProviding Compassionate Veterinary Oncology Care to Pets\nin Leesburg, Richmond, & Springfield, VA.\nThe Oncology Service - Leesburg\nReferral Forms:\nClient Referral Form\nDVM Referral Form\nPlease View Our Curbside Procedure\nHere.\nTOS is an oncology-exclusive practice specifically dedicated to providing outstanding and compassionate service to our pets with cancer and their caretakers. We do this with expertise in advanced diagnostic techniques and all forms of cancer treatment. Within our team and in collaboration with our primary care and specialty veterinary colleagues, we assist owners of pets with cancer in determining and delivering optimal therapy.\nTOS is proud to have assembled one of the largest faculties of innovative veterinary oncology specialists within a single group. Indeed, very few hospitals including university centers approach the collective training, experience, and publication record of our doctors.\nWhy should this matter to you?\nIt means that when your pet comes to TOS, it will be given the highest quality care. It means that for complicated cases or at your request, your pet’s situation will be reviewed by our outstanding team to ensure that the best recommendations are made and that no stone is left unturned as we consider the options for your pet.\nExclusive Focus on Cancer\nWe don’t do vaccinations. We don’t spay or neuter. We just treat cancer, 4,000 times a year. In fact, our staff’s combined experience totals more than 100 years of oncology practice. During the course of your pet’s treatment, we call on that experience countless times, for a multitude of decisions. This experience could mean the best possible outcome for your pet’s treatment. So if your pet has cancer, and you want the best odds of beating it, you’re looking in the right place. Because we know cancer.\nA Team Approach to Cancer Treatment\nOften, our patients may have multiple other providers of care including a primary-care veterinarian and/or multiple other specialists. Communicating and effectively coordinating the treatment plan is of paramount importance to us. Your oncologist can effectively be the “quarterback” of your pet’s oncology care, distributing the needed tests or treatments to the most appropriate provider.\nAccess to Unique Treatment Options\nBetween the numerous clinical trials we regularly participate in and the state-of-the-art equipment in our facilities, you have access to a number of unique options, resulting in a treatment plan that is specific to your pet.\nClinical Trials\nTOS is committed to providing the most advanced diagnostic and treatment options for our patients. Sometimes, this means going a step further and assisting in the development of those options. To that end, TOS is pleased to participate in clinical trials that seek to provide the larger veterinary community with answers and select patients with what may be their only hope for treatment.\nView Ongoing Studies\nRequest an Appointment\nInformation and Address\nOffice Hours\nMonday - Friday: 8:00 AM - 4:00 PM\nSaturday & Sunday: CLOSED\nContact Information\nleesburg@tosvets.com\n(571) 209-1176\nAddress\n134 Fort Evans Rd NE\nLeesburg VA 20176\nSocial Links\nOur Team\nMeet Our Skilled Team\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\nDr. Pamela White\nVeterinary Radiation Oncologist\nDr. Tony Rusk\nAssociate Veterinarian (Oncology)\nDr. Christina Manley\nVeterinary Medical Oncologist\nWe Specialize in Oncology Services For Pets.\nClick below to see highlights from our diagnostics and treatment offerings for dogs and cats. Some services may not be available at all locations. Please contact us if you are seeking a service or treatment not listed.\nsee more\nrequest an appointment\nDiagnostics and Treatments\nDiagnostics and Treatments\nMedical Oncology\nRadiation Oncology\nDiagnostic Imaging\nStereotactic Radiation Therapy\nVisit our office to get the latest in top-quality veterinary care along with unparalleled service\nLinks\nAbout Us\nServices\nResources\nContact Us\nPrivacy Policy\nAccessibility\nLogin / Account\nGet In Touch\nTOS - Leesburg\n(571) 209-1176\nleesburg@tosvets.com\nTOS - Richmond\n(804) 999-0001\nrichmond@tosvets.com\nTOS - Springfield\n(703) 451-8900, option 2\nspringfield@tosvets.com\nHow Are We Doing?\nReview Us\nfacebook\ninstagram\nX\nThe Oncology Service - Springfield\nThe Oncology Service - Richmond\nThe Oncology Service - Leesburg\n©2025 The Oncology Service. Resource Articles ©2025 KARMAjack. All Rights Reserved.\nVeterinary websites by KARMAjack\nNotice\nTemporary Closure Notice\nOur hospital will be closed from\nSeptember 8–12\nfor unexpected facility repairs.\nWe’re working quickly to get everything resolved. In the meantime, our team will be monitoring our email and voicemail remotely.\nThank you for your patience and understanding, we can’t wait to welcome you and your pets back soon!\nSee other locations\nDismiss",
